evidence = "The exact candidate revision, build and verification commands, exit codes and private logs are recorded by reference to /out/run/gates.jsonl. The final response copies the last bounded gate evidence. No file is amended after qualification."
baseline = "No baseline gate: implementation precedes the declared hf-build and hf-done qualification."
implementation = "The native from_captured adapter matches ExecutionError::Fault(ExecutionFault::EngineFault) with the complete producer reason program replay record refused: Bounds as -740 before mapping other Fault variants to -741. Other variants remain -3; publish_replay_record and the missing-record refusal retain their existing behavior."
replay_bound = "profiled_capture_one_byte_above_its_bound_answers_replay_bound executes the real budgeted CALL, derives a profile one byte smaller than its actual canonical record, asserts the exact from_captured producer refusal and observes -740 from the native adapter."
guest_trap = "trapping_guest_initializer_retains_failure_and_replay_record executes an unreachable initializer with a replay profile, asserts an Ok record with a Failure outcome and present replay record, and observes the entire unchanged record through from_captured."
engine_fault = "with_trace_policy applies TracePolicy::new(2, 128) after ProgramReplayProfile::new(128, 1048576) to the real executor, asserts ExecutionError::Fault(ExecutionFault::EngineFault) with the exact reason program replay profile and trace policy diverged, and observes -741 from the native adapter."
compatibility = "unprofiled_call_and_retained_guest_failure_are_unchanged preserves complete successful and failed unprofiled records, absence of capture, and frozen 39 CPU usage; other_execution_variants_keep_non_canonical drives a real missing-entrypoint refusal and asserts -3. Retained guest terminal failures remain typed outcomes rather than executor errors."
registry = "native_kernel_resolves_both_status_names invokes the declared C codec executable in its replay-status-names mode and asserts both exact names emitted by the actual lxp_result_name. result_replay_and_engine_codes_named checks both values, exact names, module domains and nonfatal classification in C. The Go registry parity gate consumes address-table section (b), also used by the Rust SDK result generator; Python declares both codes non-retryable."
environment = "The gate executes local Wasm, budget admission, capture and the production native status adapter without host callbacks, credentials, environment variables, live endpoints, subprocess compilation, mocks or generated fixture projects."
qualification_note = "The first build refused concat! in a link attribute; the retry rejected a direct archive link. The final repair transports actual registry names from the C codec executable built by the verify command rather than linking it into the Rust test. The C entry point now runs every registered case with no arguments, as the declared gate invokes it; named selection remains. Those attempt-1 failures are recorded in the supplied continuation ruling; this attempt records its final candidate gates in /out/run/gates.jsonl."
adapter = "The public native_result module is unconditional; the real FFI execute site calls its from_captured adapter. ffi_call.rs retains its committed layout, with both plain and whitespace-insensitive diffs below thirty lines. LXP_ERR_ENGINE_FAULT / LXP_ENGINE_FAULT replace the superseded guest-fault spelling in every declared code table and contract; guest traps remain retained records."
continuation = "Attempt 3 preserves the attempt-2 runtime, C checks and six Rust tests. The missing LXP_XWEB_INVALID_PAYLOAD row now matches the existing Go registry entry for SDK xweb code 26, invalid storage receipt payload, Retryable no; the inventory and generated Python retry table carry it, and the xweb address-table wiring request is fulfilled. Final candidate build and verify results are referenced in /out/run/gates.jsonl; no post-gate edits are required."
continuation_4 = "Attempt 4 preserves the attempt-3 implementation and changes only the unknown sentinel in TestLXPRevertTable from the newly assigned -740 to unassigned -742. The 1, -9, -99 and -999 unknown checks and the -1000 and -1004 empty-name assertions remain intact. Final candidate hf-build and full hf-done results, including the C, Rust, Go, host-name and Python gates, are recorded by reference in /out/run/gates.jsonl."
